      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "cae0b1d170514bf4a0487"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\nval flightRdd = spark.sparkContext.textFile(\"dbfs:/FileStore/tables/suankiData/flight_data/2011_summary.csv\")\nval firstRow = flightRdd.first\n\nval finalflightRdd = flightRdd.filter(row => row !=firstRow && !row.trim.contains(\"Eustatius\")).map(row => row.split(\",\"))",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "6d8af9ab4af94c0c88800"
    },
    {
      "text": "In addition to the Resilient Distributed Dataset (RDD) interface, the second kind of low-level\nAPI in Spark is two types of “distributed shared variables”:\n     These  variables you can use in your user-defined functions (e.g., in a map\nfunction on an RDD or a DataFrame) that have special properties when running on a cluster.\n\n1. **broadcast variables**: broadcast variables let you save a large value on all the worker nodes and reuse it across\nmany Spark actions without re-sending it to the cluster. \n      Broadcast variables are shared, immutable variables that are cached on every machine in the cluster instead of serialized with every single task. \n\n2. **accumulators**:  accumulators let you add declare a variable and shared across the machine so that updating a\nvalue inside of a variety of transformations and propagating that value to the driver node in an\nefficient and fault-tolerant way. (e.g.,\nto implement a counter so you can see how many of your job’s input records failed to parse)\n\n  Accumulators provide a mutable variable that a Spark cluster can safely update on a per-row\nbasis. ",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "aad052e09b9e461694f22"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n// in Scala\nimport scala.collection.mutable.ArrayBuffer\nimport org.apache.spark.util.AccumulatorV2\n\n\nval arr = ArrayBuffer[BigInt]()\n\n\nclass EvenAccumulator extends AccumulatorV2[BigInt, BigInt] {\n      private var num:BigInt = 0\n      \n      def reset(): Unit = {\n          this.num = 0\n      } \n      \n      def add(intValue: BigInt): Unit = {\n          if (intValue % 2 == 0) {\n      this.num += intValue\n        }\n      } \n      def merge(other: AccumulatorV2[BigInt,BigInt]): Unit = {\n          this.num += other.value\n      } \n      def value():BigInt = {\n         this.num\n      } \n      def copy(): AccumulatorV2[BigInt,BigInt] = {\n         new EvenAccumulator\n      } \n      def isZero():Boolean = {\n         this.num == 0\n      }\n} \n\nval acc = new EvenAccumulator\nval newAcc = sc.register(acc, \"evenAcc\")\n\nacc.value \n\nflights.foreach(flight_row => acc.add(flight_row.count))\nacc.value ",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
